# Deploy always

After finishing a user-requested fix or feature in this repo, deploy without waiting to be asked again.

## Deploy steps

1. Commit relevant code changes (never `env.env`, secrets, or debug-only scripts unless explicitly requested).
2. Rebase/pull if `main` is behind `origin/main`, resolve conflicts, then `git push origin main`.
3. Render auto-deploys from `main` — confirm push succeeded and briefly tell the user deploy is building.

## Exceptions

- Do not deploy if the user only asked a question / review with no code changes.
- Do not deploy incomplete work the user asked to hold or keep local.
- Never force-push `main`.
